{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusSymbol","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorusSymbol","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.symbol_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.symbol_mul","kind":"theorem","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusSymbol.lean#L280-L294","doc":"**QDM-2 principal symbol is multiplicative (over a domain).**\n`symbol (P·Q) = symbol P · symbol Q`.  This is the associated-graded\nring-hom property of the principal-symbol map — the leading term of a\nproduct is the (twisted) product of the leading terms.  The `[IsDomain A]`\nhypothesis is exactly what keeps the leading coefficient nonzero (so the\ntop degree is `leadDeg P + leadDeg Q`, not lower). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.topDeg_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.topDeg_mul","kind":"theorem","line":247,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusSymbol.lean#L247-L278","doc":"**QDM-2 order additivity (over a domain).**  `topDeg (P·Q) = topDeg P + topDeg Q`\nfor nonzero `P`, `Q`: the leading coefficients do not annihilate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.coeffAt_mul_eq_zero_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.coeffAt_mul_eq_zero_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusSymbol.lean#L228-L245","doc":"**QDM-2 vanishing lemma:** above the sum of top degrees the product's\ncoefficients vanish (holds over any `CommRing`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.coeffAt_mul_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.coeffAt_mul_add","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusSymbol.lean#L168-L226","doc":"**QDM-2 leading-coefficient product law (holds over any `CommRing`).**\nThe coefficient of `P·Q` at the sum of top degrees is the *twisted* product\nof the leading coefficients: `coeffAt (P·Q) (m+n) = coeffAt P m · σᵐ(coeffAt Q n)`.\nThe twist `σᵐ = ofAdd m • ·` is the graded structure constant that survives\ninto the associated graded ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.toAdd_le_of_mem_support","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.toAdd_le_of_mem_support","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusSymbol.lean#L159-L166","doc":"A support exponent is bounded by any upper bound on `topDeg`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.leadCoeff_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.leadCoeff_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusSymbol.lean#L146-L155","doc":"A nonzero element has a nonzero leading coefficient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.topDeg_eq_leadDeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.topDeg_eq_leadDeg","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusSymbol.lean#L135-L144","doc":"For a **nonzero** `P`, the order filtration degree is genuinely an integer,\nequal to `leadDeg P`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.support_nonempty_of_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.support_nonempty_of_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusSymbol.lean#L129-L133","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.topDeg_Lgen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.topDeg_Lgen","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusSymbol.lean#L123-L125","doc":"`L` has order `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.topDeg_emb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.topDeg_emb","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusSymbol.lean#L118-L121","doc":"`emb a` has order `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.symbol_Lgen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.symbol_Lgen","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusSymbol.lean#L114-L116","doc":"The symbol of `L` is `L` (order `1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.symbol_emb","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.symbol_emb","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusSymbol.lean#L109-L112","doc":"The symbol of the order-`0` coefficient embedding `emb a` is itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.symbol_monomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.symbol_monomial","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusSymbol.lean#L104-L107","doc":"**QDM-1 core:** the symbol of a monomial is itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.leadCoeff_monomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.leadCoeff_monomial","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusSymbol.lean#L100-L102","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.leadDeg_monomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.leadDeg_monomial","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusSymbol.lean#L97-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.leadDeg_of_topDeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.leadDeg_of_topDeg","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusSymbol.lean#L92-L95","doc":"If `topDeg P = m` (an integer, not `⊥`) then `leadDeg P = m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.symbol_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.symbol_zero","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusSymbol.lean#L89-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.leadCoeff_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.leadCoeff_zero","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusSymbol.lean#L86-L87","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.leadDeg_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.leadDeg_zero","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusSymbol.lean#L83-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.symbol","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.symbol","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusSymbol.lean#L78-L81","doc":"**Principal symbol** of `P`: the leading `L`-monomial\n`L^(leadDeg P) · leadCoeff P`.  For the order filtration by top `L`-degree,\nthis is the image of `P` in the associated graded ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.leadCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.leadCoeff","kind":"def","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusSymbol.lean#L75-L76","doc":"**Leading coefficient** of `P`: its coefficient at the top `L`-degree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.leadDeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.QuantumTorus.leadDeg","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/QuantumTorusSymbol.lean#L71-L73","doc":"**Leading `L`-degree** of `P` as an integer (`0` for `P = 0`, which is\nharmless: the leading coefficient there is `0` as well). ","signatureChunk":0}]}